       "status": "in-design",
       "prd": "# Farrowing\n\n## Problem\n\nWorkers record each sow's farrowing as it happens — born, alive, dead — and lock it when she is done, so counts downstream (piglet processing, weaning) start from a fixed Born.\n\n## Who\n\nFarrowing-room workers, gloved, one hand, interrupted; a supervisor ending the task for the batch.\n\n## Anchor\n\nThe sow: awaiting → farrowing → finished (locked); died is an exit. The task: in progress → ending → ended.\n\n## Rules\n\n- Born is fixed at the lock; it changes only through Correct born, stamped, original kept.\n- Every count change is a stamped record; nothing is overwritten.\n- End task is manual, hold-to-commit, and needs every sow finished or explained.\n\n## Scope\n\nIn: counting, deaths, finish and lock, corrections, end task. Out: fostering (its own feature), piglet processing.\n\n## Decisions\n\n- End task stays manual (to confirm with the owner).\n"
      },
